        "raw": "<p>My son and I played the Block co-op scenario at GenCon 2019.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I played Fanatic. He played Parse. Other folks played Writhe and Haka.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>It's been many months ago now, so I don't remember the mechanics details well enough to describe them. However, I was really impressed by how much the characters really \"felt like\" the characters we know and love from SotM.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Fanatic's powers, many with the same names and similar effects, led her to dive into the fray and bust heads. Parse boosted everyone. Writhe seemed almost impossible to hit.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I left very excited about getting the finished version of the game. I had the impression they expected to have a near-finished product to play test at GenCon 2020, which now certainly won't happen. :(</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Seems like my impression was overly optimistic, given the other posts I've been reading here, which makes me sad.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I've been impressed with the RPG, but honestly I don't have space in my life for an RPG. Too much effort required.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I'm hoping that Prime War will be a fresh way to play with my favorite characters and meet a few new ones.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>They keep bringing it up on The Letters Page,&nbsp;so I'll keep&nbsp;hoping.</p>",
